# Skill: Debug `bishengir-compile` (type B)

Use `scripts/debug_compile.sh` to run `bishengir-compile` on a `kernel.mlir`
with `--mlir-print-ir-before-all --mlir-print-ir-after-all` (on by default),
capture the whole log, and optionally split the dump into one `.mlir` per pass.

## How to run

```bash
# Reproduce the exact compile that failed in E2E, with full IR trace + split
scripts/debug_compile.sh kernel.mlir \
    --cmd "--enable-hivm-compile --target=Ascend910B --block-dim=8" \
    --split-dumps ir_dumps/

# Take the captured compile flags from a file (e.g. produced by the E2E skill)
scripts/debug_compile.sh kernel.mlir --cmd-file compile_cmd.txt --save-temps temps/
```

Key options: `-b/--bin`, `-c/--cmd "ARGS"` (repeatable), `--cmd-file FILE`,
`--no-print-ir`, `--save-temps DIR`, `--verify-each`, `--debug`,
`--debug-only X`, `--split-dumps DIR`, `-o/--output FILE`, `-l/--log FILE`,
`--dry-run`.

Relevant `bishengir-compile` flags (from `bishengir-compile --help`):
`--mlir-print-ir-before-all`, `--mlir-print-ir-after-all`, `--save-temps=DIR`,
`--verify-each`, `--print-pass-id`, `--inject-ir-before=`, `--inject-ir-after=`,
`--inject-ir-from-file=`, `--save-linked-ir`, `--enable-debug-info`.

The binary auto-resolves from `--bin`, `$BISHENGIR_COMPILE`, `$ASCENDNPU_IR_BIN`,
`bishengir-output/bin`, `build/install/bin`, `build/bin`, then `PATH`.

## Agent guidance

- Always pass the **exact compile command** that failed (via `--cmd`/`--cmd-file`)
  so you reproduce the real pipeline, then add tracing to see where it breaks.
- `--split-dumps DIR` gives you the IR before/after each pass; read `index.txt`,
  find the pass where the IR first goes wrong, then isolate it with the
  `debug-bishengir-opt` skill on the corresponding `*_Before_*.mlir`.
- Use `--save-temps` to keep intermediate artifacts; `--verify-each` to catch the
  first pass that produces invalid IR.
- Report the real exit code and log path; quote the failing pass and diagnostic.
